# short-description: Ultima gauge cluster image: stock boot/root + ext4 /data
# long-description: Adds a small ext4 /data partition (p3) to meta-ti-bsp's
# stock sdimage-2part-efi.wks.in, for the persistent-odometer-state
# read-only-rootfs port (see NOTES.md "read-only rootfs" groundwork).
#
# CORRECTED 2026-08-10: an earlier version of this file *replaced* p1 (the
# vfat --source bootimg-efi partition) with /data, on the reasoning that
# Falcon's fitImage-reading stage never touches it. That reasoning was right
# about the wrong stage — it covers what tiboot3.bin (the R5 SPL) does once
# it's already running, not how the ROM finds and loads tiboot3.bin on SD in
# the first place, which turns out to be exactly this vfat partition.
# Confirmed by hardware test (board produced zero LEDs / zero video with the
# p1-repurposed image, both symptoms of the ROM finding nothing to load —
# eMMC boot was unaffected, since that path uses the separate boot0 hardware
# partition, not this one) and confirmed by byte-search: building with the
# stock .wks and grepping the resulting .wic for tiboot3.bin's own bytes
# finds a full-length match at 24.09MiB, inside p1's 1-129MiB range; building
# with p1 removed, tiboot3.bin appears nowhere in the image at all. p1 is
# required for SD boot and must stay exactly as the stock template has it.
#
# Root stays partition #2, same as stock — meta-ti-foundational/recipes-ti/
# resize-rootfs's resize_rootfs.sh hardcodes `sfdisk -N 2 ... echo ",+"` to
# grow partition 2 into whatever free space follows it on first boot. With
# /data now added as a real partition 3 *after* root, that free-space grab
# would otherwise race /data for the same space — resize_rootfs.service is
# masked in tisdk-base-image.bbappend to remove that runtime partition-table
# mutation entirely, which a bounded/eventually-read-only root wants anyway.
#
# --no-fstab-update on root (2026-08-10): wic's own fstab-injection logic
# (scripts/lib/wic/plugins/imager/direct.py:update_fstab) writes a UUID=,
# LABEL=, or bare-device-path line for /data depending on the /data part
# line's own flags — but SD and eMMC are dd'd from this exact same image, so
# whichever of those wic picks is byte-identical on both, and a bare device
# path (mmcblk0 vs mmcblk1) would be flat-out wrong on the other medium
# besides. There is no per-partition "add no entry at all" flag; the only
# lever is this one, on the partition that actually owns /etc/fstab
# (confirmed by reading partition.py: it's root's own no_fstab_update that
# gates whether the computed fstab gets debugfs-written into root's ext4
# image, regardless of what /data's line requests). ultima-data-mount.bb
# mounts /data itself instead, by deriving the device from the root
# filesystem that's already resolved by the time it runs — see that
# recipe's DESCRIPTION for the full reasoning.

bootloader --timeout=3 --append="rootfstype=ext4 ${TI_WKS_BOOTLOADER_APPEND}"
part --source bootimg-efi --sourceparams="loader=${EFI_PROVIDER}" --fstype=vfat --label boot --active --align 1024 --use-uuid --fixed-size 128M
part / --source rootfs --fstype=ext4 --label root --align 1024 --use-uuid --no-fstab-update
part /data --fstype=ext4 --label data --fixed-size 16M --align 1024
